KZ2 patch 6071: bounded byte-validated shader-program memo (experimental, off by default).

Written for Project Pyrrhus. Extends Project Helghast patch 2029 by undecuple (MIT):
https://github.com/undecuple/project-helghast . Preserves the original
FNV/structural hash and PSO key tail. LD_PROGRAM_MEMO=1 enables eight FP address entries and eight VP start
entries, each with full byte validation. Each FP retains four (hash mode, VP seed) hashes. Pure FP texture-unit,
WPOS and DDY scans are reused only after byte validation; all render/window/texture state remains dynamic.
LD_PSO_MEMO=0 disables both memo implementations. LD_PROGRAM_MEMO_SHADOW=1 checks uncached hash/key and scans
on every candidate draw, rejecting mismatches. Shadow overhead is diagnostic, never a throughput measurement.
Counters every 65536 draws report reuse and validation bytes; existing 6070 timers retain component timing.

Memory is bounded: sixteen 64-KiB snapshots plus metadata, with two legacy snapshots retained. Entries use
round-robin replacement. No write-generation/coherency assumptions or shader-cache-format changes.
Host test: tools/runtime/test_shader_program_memo.c. Windows build, full host suite, visual and independent
warm/cold/route A/B gates are pending; no measured FPS gain is claimed.
